WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.327
Several resources can help you continue after the module.

00:00:03.327 --> 00:00:09.612
The original “Attention Is All You Need” paper is the historical source for the Transformer architecture,

00:00:09.612 --> 00:00:13.107
although it is more mathematical than our course treatment.

00:00:13.107 --> 00:00:19.567
The Hugging Face Transformers documentation is the practical reference for tokenizers, pipeline,

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:24.347
AutoModel classes, training utilities, and task examples.

00:00:24.347 --> 00:00:29.842
Sentence Transformers is the main reference for sentence embeddings, semantic similarity, retrieval,

00:00:29.842 --> 00:00:32.482
and reranking workflows.

00:00:32.482 --> 00:00:38.597
When exploring public model hubs, remember that model availability and rankings change continuously.

00:00:38.597 --> 00:00:45.132
Read the model card for the exact checkpoint you intend to use rather than relying on an old

00:00:45.132 --> 00:00:50.922
tutorial. As you read documentation or research papers, keep using the same questions from this module:

00:00:50.922 --> 00:00:57.587
what is the input representation, what architecture family is being used, what was the model trained to do,

00:00:57.587 --> 00:00:58.252
and how is performance evaluated?

00:00:58.252 --> 00:00:59.520
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
